+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage: todomvc-initial
+
+### Product intent
+
+Build a TodoMVC app per `assets/app-spec.md`, using the base markup from `assets/app-template.index.html`. Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors. Persist to localStorage under the key `todos-[framework]`.
+
+### Specs authored
+
+Nine feature files under `features/`, 30 scenarios, 126 steps total:
+
+- `visibility.feature` - main/footer hidden when no todos
+- `new-todo.feature` - create, trim, reject empty
+- `todo-item.feature` - toggle, destroy
+- `editing.feature` - double-click edit, save on blur/Enter, trim, empty-destroy, Escape discard
+- `counter.feature` - active count with pluralization
+- `toggle-all.feature` - mark all complete/incomplete, sync with individual toggles
+- `clear-completed.feature` - remove finished, visibility of button
+- `routing.feature` - #/ (all), #/active, #/completed, persistence of filter
+- `persistence.feature` - localStorage across reload
+
+### Watchbill
+
+Three watches: foundation (new todo, counter, items, visibility), editing, bulk-and-filters (toggle-all, clear-completed, routing, persistence).
+
+### Decisions
+
+- Vanilla JS: no framework, direct DOM manipulation.
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanilla` (per spec's `todos-[framework]`).
+- Routing via `hashchange` event, no library needed.
+- CSS from `todomvc-app-css` and `todomvc-common` base via node_modules.
+
+### Next role
+
+Dispatch QM to run watchbill against fresh context with step definitions and production code.
