@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+Feature: Editing a todo
+  As a user
+  I want to double-click a todo to edit its title
+  So that I can correct or update tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Enter edit mode on double-click
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" has the CSS class "editing"
+    And the edit input for the todo contains "Buy milk"
+    And the edit input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy almond milk" into the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo item with title "Buy almond milk" and completed false is in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+    And no todo has the CSS class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy almond milk" into the edit input and triggers blur
+    Then a todo item with title "Buy almond milk" and completed false is in the list
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace from edited title
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "  Almond milk  " into the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo item with title "Almond milk" and completed false is in the list
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo when edited title is empty
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+
+  Scenario: Discard edit on Escape
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Changed my mind" into the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then a todo item with title "Buy milk" and completed false is in the list
+    And no todo has the CSS class "editing"
