@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by status using URL routes
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows every todo
+    When the user navigates to the "All" filter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the todo "Walk dog" is visible in the list
+    And the "All" filter link has the CSS class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only incomplete todos
+    When the user navigates to the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not visible in the list
+    And the todo "Walk dog" is visible in the list
+    And the "Active" filter link has the CSS class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only finished todos
+    When the user navigates to the "Completed" filter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the todo "Walk dog" is not visible in the list
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the CSS class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Filtering persists across page reload
+    When the user navigates to the "Active" filter
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the CSS class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Hiding completed item in filtered view when toggled
+    Given the user navigates to the "Active" filter
+    When the user completes the todo "Walk dog"
+    Then the todo "Walk dog" is not visible in the list
